course: dictionary
lesson: 14814
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «The Quakers sat in silence in their meeting house.» Sitting in a meeting house points to a church group, so Quakers here means people who belong to that group.
explain: Quakers are members of a Christian group called the Religious Society of Friends. They worship mostly in silence, and they believe there is "that of God" in every person. When you see a capital Q, a church word like meeting or worship, or a school name, you can guess it is the church meaning.
explain: The name is old and informal. It may come from a joke that the early members "quake" (tremble) before God. This is an old story about where the name came from, not the main meaning, so check the context before you decide what the word means.
fact: Quakers is a plural noun. One member is a Quaker.
fact: «Quakers» means members of a Christian group called the Religious Society of Friends.
fact: Quakers worship mostly in silence and have no priests.
fact: At a «Quaker meeting», anyone may stand and speak if they feel moved.
fact: Quakers work for peace, equality and honesty.
exercise: «The Quakers sat in silence for an hour.» What are Quakers in this sentence? | Teachers who run a school for sport | Men who mend old roofs | *A group of Christian people who worship in silence | A group of people who shake with fear
exercise: At a Quaker meeting, anyone may stand and speak if they feel moved. What does this show about Quakers? | They have priests who speak for everyone | *They have no priests, so anyone can speak | They never speak at all | They only speak on Sundays in the town square
exercise: Which word is the singular of Quakers? | *Quaker | Quake | Quakes | Quakery
test: Quakers believe there is "that of God" in every person. What do Quakers believe about people? | *Each person has something of God in them | People have no link to God | Only priests have God in them | Only children have God in them
test: The name Quakers may come from a joke about trembling. What does quake mean? | Sleep deeply | Run away quickly | *Tremble | Laugh loudly
exam: Which sentence uses Quakers in its church meaning? | «The quakers shook the old floor with their feet.» | «The quakers of the cake were sweet and sticky.» | *«The Quakers met in silence in their meeting house.» | «The Quakers ate their lunch in the park.»
